        "slide": 1,
        "role": "cover",
        "subject": "A raked cutaway of two mirrored limestone exam rooms that share one glass wall. Each room is whole: a blue door, an exam table with a seated actor, a white-coated clinician on a mesh chair and a cart with a cyan screen. The two carts face each other across the glass.",
        "visual_consequence": "Without the headline, it reads as two matched rooms with the same table, actor, clinician and cart in the same mirrored places, split by one glass pane that casts a diagonal shadow on the back wall. The two cyan screens glow at equal intensity. It is a fair two-arm setup with one difference, named by the two pills. Source and render digests are unchanged since my accepted reading.",
        "weakness": "Minor. A plain pink sky band of about 150 px sits between the dek wash and the wall top. A narrow saturated cobalt strip runs along the very top edge of the frame. The kit faces are simple at native size but aren't visible at feed size.",
        "repair": "None required. At polish, either soften the cobalt strip along the top edge into the wash or remove it.",
